<title>POLAND: Polish farmers to block German border crossing.</title>
<headline>Polish farmers to block German border crossing.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group of Polish farmers in the Solidarity trade union plan to block roads at a German border crossing to protest against food imports, PAP news agency reported on Monday.</p>
<p>The blockade at Jedrzychowice, southwest Poland, is planned to start on Tuesday and last indefinitely, PAP said.</p>
<p>PAP quoted the Lower Silesia regional Solidarity leader Marian Zagorny as saying that the government had rebuffed farmer demands for protection from imported foodstuffs.</p>
<p>Zagorny said that the blockade protest was backed by other regional Solidarity groups.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
